From ad156918d04d10e62f3ceab41453103946a54beb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sirherobrine23 <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 11:11:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 125/153] net: airoha: propagate xPON link state to GDM2

The xPON provider currently updates only the GDM2 carrier state, so the netdevice phylink instance cannot report the active GPON or EPON line speed through ethtool.

Add a locked xPON link-state snapshot to the GDM device and let the provider publish mode, carrier, nominal speed, duplex, port type, and exact asymmetric line rates. Use the snapshot for ethtool link settings and reject Ethernet-style link configuration on an xPON-managed port.

Report GPON as 2.5 Gbit/s downstream with the exact 2.48832/1.24416 Gbit/s line rates retained in the snapshot, and report EPON as symmetric 1 Gbit/s. Add the 1 Gbit/s capability required by EPON to the internal GDM2 phylink configuration.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
